 ## `diff(obj1, obj2)`
 
-Compare two objects with nested [serialization](#serializeinput-options). Returns an array of changes.
+Compare two objects with nested [serialization](#serializeinput). Returns an array of changes.
 
-The returned value is an array of diff entries with `$key`, `$hash`, `$value`, and `$props`. When logging, a string version of the changelog is displayed.
+Each entry in the returned array has:
+
+- `key`: the dotted path of what changed (`""` at the root)
+- `type`: `"added"`, `"removed"` or `"changed"`
+- `newValue`: the new node, absent on a `"removed"` entry
+- `oldValue`: the previous node, absent on an `"added"` entry
+
+A node carries `key`, `value` (the value itself), `hash` (its serialized form,
+or a `{...}` summary for a container) and, for a container, `props` mapping each
+key to its own node.
+
+Entries stringify to a readable line, so logging a changelog needs no formatting
+of your own.
 
